> xt(x: u8) = ((x << 1) & 0xff) xor ((x & 0x80) != 0 ? 0x1b : 0)
> gm(a: u8, b: u8) = ((b&1)!=0?a:0) xor ((b&2)!=0?xt(a):0) xor ((b&4)!=0?xt(xt(a)):0) xor ((b&8)!=0?xt(xt(xt(a))):0) xor ((b&16)!=0?xt(xt(xt(xt(a)))):0) xor ((b&32)!=0?xt(xt(xt(xt(xt(a))))):0) xor ((b&64)!=0?xt(xt(xt(xt(xt(xt(a)))))):0) xor ((b&128)!=0?xt(xt(xt(xt(xt(xt(xt(a))))))):0)
> gmr(a: u8, b: u8) = gm(b, a)
> equiv gm gmr
gm and gmr are equal on the domain of gm (exhaustive)
> range xt
range of xt -> u8:
  0..255   (256 distinct values)
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range gm
range of gm -> u8:
  0..255   (256 distinct values)
  fits in u8
  over all 65536 points of the domain
> id8(x: u8) = x
> mul_one(x: u8) = gm(x, 1)
> equiv mul_one id8
mul_one and id8 are equal on the domain of mul_one (exhaustive)
> mul_zero(x: u8) = gm(x, 0)
> zz(x: u8) = 0
> equiv mul_zero zz
mul_zero and zz are equal on the domain of mul_zero (exhaustive)
> assoc1(a: u8, b: u8, c: u8) = gm(gm(a,b),c)
> assoc2(a: u8, b: u8, c: u8) = gm(a,gm(b,c))
> equiv assoc1 assoc2
assoc1 and assoc2 are equal on the domain of assoc1 (sampled, not proved; SAT gave up on 1173 AIG nodes within its budget of 100000 conflicts or 100000000 steps)
